``` Discovery burst: many different enumeration tools, one host, one account, ten minutes.
    Platform: Splunk. Not run against a live instance.

    Why native and not Sigma: Sigma filters one event at a time. This counts how many
    DIFFERENT tools an account ran close together, which needs an aggregation Sigma cannot
    express. The tool list is taken from the "Enumeration of the Environment" section
    of CISA AA23-144A.

    Windowing: streamstats time_window is a true sliding window, so a burst that
    straddles a clock boundary (12:09 and 12:11) is still counted together. It needs
    events in time order, hence the sort.

    Replace the first line with your own process-creation search. Field names follow
    the Sigma convention (Image, CommandLine, User) used by the generated queries;
    map them to your sourcetype. ```
<your process-creation search> earliest=-30d
| eval tool=lower(mvindex(split(Image, "\\"), -1))
| search tool IN ("arp.exe", "dnscmd.exe", "ipconfig.exe", "ldifde.exe", "net.exe",
    "net1.exe", "netsh.exe", "netstat.exe", "nltest.exe", "reg.exe", "systeminfo.exe",
    "tasklist.exe", "wevtutil.exe", "whoami.exe", "wmic.exe")
| sort 0 _time
| streamstats time_window=10m dc(tool) AS tool_count values(tool) AS tools BY host User
| where tool_count >= 5
| stats max(tool_count) AS tool_count values(tools) AS tools
    earliest(_time) AS first_seen latest(_time) AS last_seen BY host User
| convert ctime(first_seen) ctime(last_seen)
| sort - tool_count
